  "narrative": {
    "act_1_pitch": "The promoter asked for EUR 725,000 to reopen the caseron as an 8-key hotel with a 21-cover restaurant, on 19.2% occupancy and an EUR 85 ADR. The model reproduces EUR 86,275 of Year-1 revenue and EUR 11,297 of EBITDA - but with no variable cost stack and negative Year-1 cash.",
    "act_2_audit": "A full cost stack, INE Segovia seasonality, the Segovia hospitality agreement and the 21% VAT bridge raise the all-in budget to EUR 1,050,100. The best demand case (31.36% occupancy) generates EUR 171,720 of mature revenue and a 1.15x minimum DSCR.",
    "act_3_decline": "The credit committee declines: the Year-2 DSCR is 1.15x against a 1.25x covenant, the equity plug is EUR 521k (49.6% of all-in CapEx), the restaurant does not cover its fixed cost, and Phase II opens a EUR 252k hole.",
    "act_4_turnaround": "Six modular cabins at EUR 93,600 installed plus the caseron as a four-bedroom lodge cut the cash envelope to EUR 621,600 (-40% versus the EUR 1,050,100 audited budget). No commercial kitchen, two FTE, EUR 358,062 of mature revenue at a 30.8% EBITDA margin and a 2.31x minimum DSCR.",
    "act_5_comparison": "On a like-for-like 3%-cost exit at an 8.5% cap rate the T8 equity IRR is 19.0% all-in and 39.7% on cash equity, against -24.4% for the audited case. The turnaround creates EUR 385,869 of value over its all-in CapEx; the audited case destroys EUR 627,390."
  },
